## Rows and columns

A slide is one column by default: **title, text, code**, top left. Two tags change that. A `<row>` puts its children **side by side**
and divides the width between them; a `<col>` **stacks** its children. Nest them for any layout, and the parts always add up to
the whole slide.

<code lang=text>
  ## Title                     <- loose text on top

  <row>                        <- below it, side by side:
    The text on the left
    <code lang=ts>...\</code>   <- the code on the right
  \</row>

  <row>
    <col>a <img src=x.png />\</col>   <- a col: several things in one part
    b
    <text size=2>c\</text>          <- twice as wide
  \</row>
</code>

Every direct child of a row is a part (loose text between tags is one part). `size=2` is a weight, `size=auto` the size of the
content, `size=40%` a length. Add `halign` or `valign` to align inside a part.

<notes>
  Slide settings: layout: cover for a title slide. margin: and gap: in the slide block set the space around and between the parts.
</notes>
